    "null_method": "IMPORTANT DATA-AVAILABILITY NOTE: the literal protocol (permute pos/neg labels within each of the 3 stability sets' own per-sample hidden states, recompute mean-diff vectors, cosine between them) could not be run as specified because scripts/04_stability.py deletes each set's raw per-sample states.npz after computing the axis vector (only data/stability/deepseek_r1_14b_set_C_states.npz survives, from an interrupted run -- not enough for a real cross-set null on any model). Substitute: for each model/axis, 1000 permutations draw two INDEPENDENT Rademacher sign vectors over that model's own main-calibration paired pos/neg diffs (data/axes/<model>_hidden_states.npz, train+val pooled, n_pairs = n_train+n_val, same construction as scripts/06d_axis_geometry.py), form null_vec_k = mean(sign_k * diff_i), and take cosine(null_vec_1, null_vec_2). This uses real per-sample activations from the same model/axis (not fabricated), just a different question set (the main 65-question calibration set rather than the 3 stability sets)."
